\description{
The model families were renamed to a single \verb{cogmod_*} scheme, so that every
family reads as one of this package's and none of them can collide with a
\code{brms} or \code{stats} name. The old names still work and are exact synonyms, but
they are no longer documented and will be removed in a future release.\tabular{ll}{
   old \tab new \cr
   \code{rt_lognormal()} \tab \code{cogmod_lognormal()} \cr
   \code{rt_loggamma()} \tab \code{cogmod_loggamma()} \cr
   \code{rt_invgaussian()} \tab \code{cogmod_invgaussian()} \cr
   \code{rt_gamma()} \tab \code{cogmod_gamma()} \cr
   \code{rt_invgamma()} \tab \code{cogmod_invgamma()} \cr
   \code{rt_weibull()} \tab \code{cogmod_weibull()} \cr
   \code{rt_invweibull()} \tab \code{cogmod_invweibull()} \cr
   \code{rt_logweibull()} \tab \code{cogmod_logweibull()} \cr
   \code{rt_exgaussian()} \tab \code{cogmod_exgaussian()} \cr
   \code{rt_lba()} \tab \code{cogmod_lba1()} \cr
   \code{lba()} \tab \code{cogmod_lba2()} \cr
   \code{lnr()} \tab \code{cogmod_lnr()} \cr
   \code{rdm()} \tab \code{cogmod_rdm()} \cr
   \code{ddm()} \tab \code{cogmod_ddm()} \cr
   \code{choco()} \tab \code{cogmod_choco()} \cr
   \code{betagate()} \tab \code{cogmod_betagate()} \cr
   \code{betadiscrete()} \tab \code{cogmod_betadiscrete()} \cr
}


Every derived function follows its family: \code{rrt_lognormal()} is
\code{rcogmod_lognormal()}, \code{rt_lognormal_stanvars()} is
\code{cogmod_lognormal_stanvars()}, and so on for the density, the \verb{*_stanvars()},
the \verb{*_lpdf_expose()} and the \code{brms} post-processing hooks.
}
